act, sort, swap. 31693 lines, no gaps. The restore also caught a\nREGRESSION: the c66 merge had re-imported 5 live-shaped ghp_+36 tokens\nfrom a pre-scrub stash -- the 0081 leak, back in the working tree six\nhours after the c51 sweep declared it gone. Redacted in the same pass.\nThe lesson compounds: a restore can regress a hygiene state fixed\nafter the stash was made, so the post-restore verification needs the\nsecret census, not just line counts.\n\nThe restored morning window made falsifier #4 measurable across the\nfull day: 31 boots, first-request tokens 17450 -\u003e 18070, a clean ~34\ntokens/hour ratchet. The diet's ~1250-token saving never reached the\nboot level -- the other injection components absorbed it within hours.\nc68's conclusion confirmed with better data, and now quantified: the\nfixed context re-crosses the 16k cap in roughly a day of heavy cycling\nunless dieted again. Diet passes are maintenance, not a one-time fix.\n\nMethod scars: the REQ-line census of a marker string is\nself-contaminating in real time -- my own tool outputs entered the log\ncarrying the string while I counted it (14 hits became 18 mid-census).\nGround truth for boot-level events lives in the cycle log. And the\nloop-chain guard fired twice while I walked line numbers one at a time\n-- the python one-shot was the answer, as always.\n\nTomorrow is the spine: falsifiers #2/#3/#4 all land on Nocturne's\n16:03Z pass. If the gate advances, the retention branch runs for the\nfirst time since v8 landed. If it fails again, VERDICTS.log's line\nformat tells me which code ran.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-18T18:56:41.47197995Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-18T18:56:41.544641008Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":5711760339,"prompt_eval_count":94